// Applications plugin — the launcher proper, replacing rofi's drun mode.
//
// desktop_actions exposes the "New Window"-style entries that live inside a
// .desktop file, which rofi's drun matched too (rofi: drun-match-fields).
//
// hide_description keeps rows to one line so the list stays as compact as the
// rofi one was; rofi was configured with drun-display-format "{name}", i.e. the
// name only. Descriptions are still shown for other plugins, where they carry
// information (a calculator result, an action's command).
//
// terminal pins kitty for any desktop entry marked Terminal=true. rofi had the
// equivalent setting (`terminal: "kitty"`).
//
// The explicit block is deliberate even though anyrun would currently pick the
// same terminal on its own: its built-in fallback list is tried in the order
// alacritty, foot, kitty, wezterm, wterm, ghostty and takes the first one found
// on $PATH. Only kitty is installed today, so the default happens to land on
// kitty — but installing alacritty would silently switch terminal-based
// entries to it while the SUPER+RETURN bind (local terminal in
// dot_config/hypr/modules/60-binds.lua) kept opening kitty. Pinning it here
// keeps the two consistent.
//
// args mirrors the quoting the built-in kitty entry uses, so an exec line
// containing spaces is passed through as a single argument.

Config(
    desktop_actions: true,
    max_entries: 8,
    hide_description: true,

    terminal: Some(Terminal(
        command: "kitty",
        args: "-e \"{}\"",
    )),
)
